# No barrel files

Do not add `index.ts` / `index.js` files that only re-export from sibling modules.

## Why

Barrel files force bundlers to load every re-exported module. In Next.js App Router that can pull client-only code into Server Components.

## Instead

- Import from the concrete module or package subpath
- Publish subpath `exports` in `package.json` (e.g. `@elirobinson/react/components/*`) — no root `"."` barrel
- Name implementation files by purpose (`tokens-data.ts`), not `index.ts`

## Allowed exceptions

- Storybook / Vite aliases that map `@design-system/*` to `src/*`
- A single-module folder where `index.ts` contains the implementation (not re-exports)

```typescript
// Bad
export { Button } from './components/atoms/Button';

// Good
import { Button } from '@elirobinson/react/components/atoms/Button';
import { tokens } from '@elirobinson/tokens/tokens-data';
```
